# This file contains a list of files that will be excluded from Shopify CLI
# operations such as push, pull, dev, etc.
#
# Examples:
#
# Ignore a specific file:
#   templates/product.json
#
# Ignore templates with a wildcard pattern:
#   templates/*.json
#
# Ignore templates and sections with a regular expression:
#   /(templates|sections)/.*\.json/

# Demo store tooling (§12). None of this is part of the distributable theme —
# it seeds the developer's own demo store and builds the buyer's export
# package. Listing it here keeps `shopify theme push` and `shopify theme
# package` to the theme itself.
scripts/
demo-media-raw/
demo-media/
demo-store-export/
store-submission-build/
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
.env*

# Internal build/dev documentation — not part of the distributable theme.
# Listed individually rather than as a `*.md` + `!` negation pair.
# Verified against an actual `shopify theme package` output: root-level
# .md files (README.md, LICENSE.md, CRO-CHECKLIST.md) never appear in the
# zip regardless of what's in this file — `theme package` only scans the
# theme's own folders (assets/, config/, layout/, locales/, sections/,
# snippets/, templates/), so root files were never going to ship through
# it either way, and a `!` negation had nothing to re-include. Those three
# reach a buyer some other way (the repo, the store listing) — not this
# zip. assets/LICENSES.md ships automatically, since it already lives
# inside assets/.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE-TASKS-theme-store-fixes.md
loam-theme-store-fixes.md
DEMO-SCREENSHOTS.md
FUTURE-ENHANCEMENTS.md
PROGRESS.md
RELEASE-NOTES.md
TEST-CASES.md
THEME-STORE-CHECKLIST.md
.githooks/
.github/
.theme-check.yml
